ROLLBACK Demonstration

Objective: To demonstrate how PostgreSQL reverses uncommitted database changes.

Scenario: A product's inventory stock was reduced by 5 units within a transaction.

SQL commands used:

BEGIN to initiate the transaction.
UPDATE to reduce product stock.
ROLLBACK to reverse the update.
SELECT to verify the final stock quantity.

Result: The stock quantity remained unchanged after executing ROLLBACK.

Conclusion: This demonstrates how PostgreSQL transactions protect data integrity by allowing uncommitted changes to be reversed.

